  "hindi": "इसकी सेवा करते हुए भृगुओं ने उसे जलों के सहवास-स्थान में, आयु की बस्तियों में, दूसरी बार स्थापित किया। यह बहुलता सब पर छा जाए; देवों का परिचारक, तीव्र घोड़ों वाला अग्नि।",
  "english": "Worshipping this one, the Bhṛgus placed him a second time in the common seat of the waters, among the clans of Āyu. May this abundance prevail over all things: Agni, the attendant of the gods, with swift horses.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "The first half-verse has no explicit 'Agni'; imam is taken as Agni from the second line. 'Āyu' is read as a name (alternatively 'of man'). The construction of the second line is unclear: eṣa ... bhūmā 'this abundance' is taken as subject of abhy astu, with Agni in apposition; the alternative is eṣa = Agni as subject and bhūmā as an adverbial 'in abundance'. arati (attendant) is uncertain. apāṃ sadhasthe 'in the common seat of the waters' is rendered literally.",
  "confidence": "low",
  "type": "verse",
  "line_ids": [
   "002.004.2a",
   "002.004.2b"
  ],
  "lines_deva": [
