  "hindi": "देवों ने मानव बस्तियों में अग्नि को प्रिय स्थापित किया, बसने को उद्यत जनों की भाँति, मित्र को। वह उत्सुक रातों में चमके, जो बल के योग्य है, दानी के घर में।",
  "english": "The gods placed Agni as one dear among the human clans, like those about to settle, a friend. May he shine through the eager nights, he who is worthy of vigour, in the house of the giver.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "dhuḥ is a syncopated perfect (= dadhuḥ) of √dhā. ūrmyā 'night' and the sense of uśatīḥ 'eager' are uncertain; dakṣāyya is uncertain (taken as 'worthy of vigour'); the final ā after dame is left as a separate particle. The comparison 'like a friend about to settle' is the literal reading. Correction: kṣeṣyantaḥ is nominative plural and cannot agree with mitram (acc. sg.); the literal reading is 'like those about to settle, a friend'.",
  "confidence": "low",
  "type": "verse",
  "line_ids": [
   "002.004.3a",
   "002.004.3b"
  ],
  "lines_deva": [
   "अ॒ग्निं दे॒वासो॒ मानु॑षीषु वि॒क्षु प्रि॒यं धु॑: क्षे॒ष्यन्तो॒ न मि॒त्रम्",
   "स दी॑दयदुश॒तीरूर्म्या॒ आ द॒क्षाय्यो॒ यो दास्व॑ते॒ दम॒ आ"
  ],
  "lines_iast": [
   "a̱gniṃ de̱vāso̱ mānṷṣīṣu vi̱kṣu pri̱yaṃ dhṷ: kṣe̱ṣyanto̱ na mi̱tram",
   "sa dī̭dayaduśa̱tīrūrmyā̱ ā da̱kṣāyyo̱ yo dāsva̭te̱ dama̱ ā"
  ],
